mruby 4.0.0-rc2: RProc alignment for capability targets

src/class.c, src/proc.c and mruby-catch declare their static RProc constants
with mrb_alignas(8). On a target whose pointers are capabilities, RProc holds
one, so its minimum alignment is 16, and a declared alignment BELOW the type's
own is an error rather than a hint:

  src/class.c:4240: error: requested alignment is less than minimum alignment
  of 16 for type 'const struct RProc'

The CHERI compiler refuses it, so mruby does not build for CheriBSD purecap at
all. master carries the same mrb_alignas(8) at every one of these sites, so
this is not a pin artifact and there is no upstream fix to backport.

Asking for the type's own alignment, or 8 where that is larger, keeps the
original intent -- these constants are reached through tagged pointers and must
not be under-aligned -- and is correct on both kinds of target without a
platform conditional. _Alignof is a constant expression in C11, so the
conditional is a valid _Alignas argument.

The Capstone domain build does not need this patch: its compiler accepts the
narrower declaration. It lives here rather than in ../app/patches so that the
domain arms' images stay byte-for-byte what their measurements were taken on --
build-mruby-domain.sh applies every patch in that directory.

diff --git i/mrbgems/mruby-catch/src/catch.c w/mrbgems/mruby-catch/src/catch.c
index 4acbd822c..40dc1fb55 100644
--- i/mrbgems/mruby-catch/src/catch.c
+++ w/mrbgems/mruby-catch/src/catch.c
@@ -46,7 +46,7 @@ static const mrb_irep catch_irep = {
 };
 
 /* Procedure object for catch method - used to identify catch blocks in call stack */
-mrb_alignas(8)
+mrb_alignas(_Alignof(struct RProc) > 8 ? _Alignof(struct RProc) : 8)
 static const struct RProc catch_proc = {
   NULL, MRB_TT_PROC, MRB_GC_RED, MRB_OBJ_IS_FROZEN, MRB_PROC_SCOPE | MRB_PROC_STRICT,
   { &catch_irep }, NULL, { NULL }
